Use Unreal Engine 5 as the primary 3D engine and rendering runtime.

Target the visual quality of AAA games, premium architectural visualization and cinematic environments.

Utilize the following technologies where supported:

- Nanite Virtualized Geometry.
- Lumen Global Illumination.
- Lumen Reflections.
- Hardware Ray Tracing.
- Virtual Shadow Maps.
- Temporal Super Resolution.
- Physically Based Rendering.
- High-resolution PBR materials.
- 4K and 8K textures where appropriate.
- Volumetric lighting.
- Realistic indirect lighting.
- Physically accurate shadows.
- Contact shadows.
- Reflection systems.
- Ambient occlusion.
- Cinematic depth of field.
- Filmic tone mapping.
- Dynamic exposure adaptation.
- High-quality anti-aliasing.
- Subtle bloom.
- Cinematic color grading.
- Unreal Engine Movie Render Queue for cinematic previews.
- OpenXR for immersive VR experiences.

Use professional assets from Fab, Megascans and other appropriately licensed external 3D asset libraries.

Download, install, configure and integrate any compatible external libraries, plugins, shaders, textures, 3D models, rendering frameworks and dependencies necessary to achieve the highest possible visual quality.

Do not limit the project to default engine assets or basic procedural geometry.

Do not use low-poly furniture, primitive chairs, cartoonish environments, flat textures or unrealistic placeholder objects.

Every architectural element must appear professionally designed and physically believable.

